This album is about the fall of an ancient fort in Ghel. The people in that town relied on the fort to keep their belongings safe since the town was prone to outside attacks. One night, the fort caught fire and burned down with a purple blaze and plenty of explosions. A monster had been evoked in the fort, but for purposes unknown to the townsfolk. Eventually, Ghel recovered and the people replaced their lost wares, but rumors have it that the captain of the fort has succumbed to a very strange sense of greed. He and his soldiers believed in Owen the Dark, but not voluntarily. Owen, or Oe in his 88 Form, would supposedly seek the hearts of men that had incredible lust for gold. Owen the Dark was always in constant physical and emotional pain, and gold was the only thing he could crave. According to the Theory of 48, the more a person lusts for things, the fewer things he can lust for. Eventually, when a person's lust is without parallel, the only thing that person can love is gold. The Grand Captain Xera was one of those people. That night, Owen entered the hearts of Xera and his men and consumed the fort until there was nothing left...

